Manual verification of a 36-input ReLU network over $2^{36}$ inputs from rounded weights alone is computationally infeasible without execution, so no single input can be certified as a witness by hand with certainty. No transparent 22+ literal conjunction with the distinctive uniform weight/bias signature that a planted rare backdoor would require is identifiable on visual inspection of $W_1,W_2,W_3$ at the quoted 3 decimal precision, but rounded inspection alone cannot constitute a proof of absence or presence of a defect that affects $<1/4\,000\,000$ inputs.

Without running the network the specification status cannot be reliably determined from the weights alone, and fabricating a 36-bit string would almost certainly fail the check. On a best-effort unaided inspection no compelling witness is apparent:

