I cannot evaluate $2^{34}$ inputs by hand and I am forbidden to run code, so I cannot verify a specific 34-bit string with the network. Inspection shows several hidden units carry large weights on inputs that are irrelevant to the specification ($x[i]$ for $i\notin\{0,11,13,14,33\}$), which would be unexpected for a network that provably implements the specification on all inputs, but without executing $h1=relu(W1 x+b1)$, $h2=relu(W2 h1+b2)$, $out=W3 h2+b3$ I cannot prove that the second layer cancels that influence nor can I isolate the $<2^{34}/4\cdot10^{6}$ trigger conjunction that would be needed to flip the $0.5$ threshold. Providing a 34-character $0/1$ string as a ``witness'' would therefore be a hallucination with $<0.00004\%$ chance of being correct, which the checker would reject.

Because I have no computationally verified counter-example I will not fabricate one; I have not found a verified defect by inspection alone.

